a  so we've been supported I mean that is a  very humbling experience  [Applause]  you know it is it is one thing to go to  Wall Street and to walk out of a  fundraiser with ten million dollars it  is another thing to get checks of $10  and $15 from people who are on Social  Security so that was just an  extraordinarily gratifying experience um  if you would ask me you know people say  well you know what was you know the most  significant thing in the campaign on a  personal level I'll tell you what it was  it was doing rallies all over the  country and on the end of the campaign  in June the last day was June 7th in  California and five other states we we  spent a lot of time in California  running up and down the state and we  held rallies in very rural areas where  presidential candidates never go and on  a beautiful evening there'd be five ten  thousand people coming out often young  Latino kids African American kids white  kids Native Americans were playing an  active role and you look out at a crowd  of such a diverse audience such a  beautiful young people who have such  hopes for this country that is what  inspired me then and that is what  inspires me today and that is what  should inspire all of you  [Applause]  what I want you to know but I want you  to know election results notwithstanding  there are millions of people in this  country who love this country  passionately who want to see this  country become what we all know it can  become and I had the opportunity a  privilege to actually see and meet with  so many of those people and that is  something that I will live with for the  rest of my life well the first half of  the book deals with the campaign and if  you're interested in politics I think  you'll find it interesting  the second half does something a little  bit different and what it says is how do  we go forward we are the wealthiest  nation in the history of the world  that's what we are today and there is no  excuse for 43 million people li